  "name": "Bhavgeet (Marathi light poetic song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bhavgeet is Marathi light song that sets modern lyric poetry, by poets such as Mangesh Padgaonkar and Shanta Shelke, to simple, raga-tinged melodies. It took shape on gramophone records in the 1930s and spread through All India Radio, shaped by composer-singers such as Sudhir Phadke, composer of the radio song-cycle Geet Ramayan, and Shrinivas Khale, and by singers such as Arun Date.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1930s bhavgeet, functional Song, south Asian pop branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. harmonium indian, tabla, low overtone rich assam bamboo bambusa tulda canonical Hindustani bansuri. blanket damped 1925-1945 commercial-major electrical era office. Neumann U47, German V72 tube pre, German tube console. tape 15ips.",
